 "notes": [
  "All mainland block edges and licence dates are taken from Traficom's 'Frequencies and licence holders of public mobile networks' page (last updated 21.9.2026).",
  "Licensing is national except for the autonomous province of Åland, which has its own licences (shown in each band's note, not drawn). Åland holdings: Ålcom (Ålands Telekommunikation Ab) 450 MHz 5 MHz, 700 2×15, 800 2×15, 900 2×17.2 (two blocks), 1800 2×37.5, 2100 2×19.8, 2600 2×35, 3.5 GHz 3700–3800 MHz; Telia (Åland) 700 2×15, 800 2×15, 900 2×17.2, 1800 2×37.3, 2100 2×19.8, 2600 2×35, 3410–3510 MHz. davwheat's separate AX dataset was not in the seed snapshot.",
  "Most licences run to 31.12.2033; the 2.6 GHz licences (FDD and TDD) expire 16.12.2029. Licence terms require the 900/1800/2100 licensees to keep 2G running until the end of 2029.",
  "Local (non-national) 4G/5G networks can be licensed in 2300–2320 MHz and 24.25–25.1 GHz; 3800–4200 MHz is being prepared for local use."
